/*
 * Delta Plus Design Tokens
 * Single source of truth for all design values
 */

:root {
  /* ===================
   * PRIMITIVE COLORS (Spec 1.0)
   * =================== */

  /* ── THE DEFAULT SURFACE FAMILY ────────────────────────────────────────────
     RETUNED 2026-08-11 (`F-PALETTE-01`). Owner: *"the dark (warm) colour looks better
     (it looks slick). But I want a not as dark version as default (but maybe darker or
     more optimised version than today's default)."* So the default is now strictly
     between the two palettes it used to sit outside: **warmer and darker than the old
     default (#262322), still clearly lighter than Dark (Warm) (#0D0B0A)** — which keeps
     a reason for Dark (Warm) to exist as a separate choice.

     HOW THESE VALUES WERE DERIVED, because "pick a nicer hex" is what failed last time.
     Each token below is Dark (Warm)'s CORRESPONDING token LIFTED in OKLab lightness by
     t=0.40 of the distance to the old default, taking Dark (Warm)'s hue exactly and
     scaling chroma with lightness so its *relative* colourfulness is preserved. One knob,
     one axis: t=0 is Dark (Warm), t=1 is the old default's lightness in Dark (Warm)'s hue.
     Moving the whole family is one regeneration, not thirteen judgement calls.

     ⚠️ ONE TOKEN IS NOT DERIVED FROM ITS OWN COUNTERPART, and the recipe above will give
     the wrong answer for it: `--sidebar-bg-*`. The two palettes disagree about which token
     the rails mirror — the old default set them from `--color-inset` (29,26,25) while
     `[data-palette="warm"]` sets them from `--color-bg` (13,11,10). This family follows the
     DEFAULT's own idiom and derives them from `--color-inset`, giving #100F0D. Feeding the
     recipe Dark (Warm)'s sidebar value instead yields #131110, which is NOT what is
     committed. Stated here because a reader regenerating from the recipe would otherwise
     silently change the rails. The underlying inconsistency predates this fold and is
     flagged for its own fold, not resolved here.

     CHOSEN BY LOOKING, not by argument. Four candidates (t = 0.70 / 0.55 / 0.40 / 0.25)
     were rendered on the real page against both designs and compared side by side, with
     each candidate applied on a FRESH LOAD — measured 2026-08-11, the Canvas2d chart
     themes resolve at mount and do NOT react to a live palette switch, so an override
     injected after mount paints honest CSS over a stale chart and would have made the
     comparison a lie. On a fresh load every canvas tracks `--color-surface` exactly.

     R−B rises across the ladder from the old default's 6,5,4,4,2 to 11,8,4,3,2 — the same
     shape as Dark (Warm)'s own 10,6,3,2,1 rather than the old flat neutral one. That IS
     the warmth. Note the range is 2–11, NOT 4–11: the two darkest steps sit at 3 and 2,
     because at those lightnesses 8-bit quantisation has almost no room left to carry hue.
     The per-token annotations below are updated rather than left stating a property this
     family no longer has.

     EVERY INK RATIO RISES; NONE FALL. Against the page: body/`--bar-ink-primary`
     13.34 → 15.67, secondary 6.58 → 7.73, muted 4.13 → 4.85, brand 5.76 → 6.76,
     focus 14.33 → 16.83. The shell pane's own surface needs no edit at all — it is
     `rgba(255,255,255,0.06)`, a lift off whatever the page is, which is precisely why
     it was built that way. ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */

  /* Gray Scale — warm charcoal (R-B=2-11, cool text grays B>R) */
  --color-gray-50:  #F5F5F7;  /* cool tint — text crispness */
  --color-gray-100: #EDEDEF;
  --color-gray-200: #d4d4d8;
  --color-gray-300: #b4b4b8;
  --color-gray-400: #A8A8AC;
  /* STEP 11(c): two AA-derived muted steps. Added, never repointed — every existing consumer of
   * gray-400/500/600 keeps the value it had. Each is the LIGHTEST/darkest value that still clears
   * 4.5:1 against the worst surface of the theme that uses it, so the muted role stays visually
   * muted rather than being lifted further than the requirement. */
  --color-gray-450: #9A9A9D;  /* dark muted — 4.53:1 on --color-surface-hover #353230 (worst dark) */
  --color-gray-500: #838386;  /* R-B=-3 — --color-muted */
  --color-gray-550: #5C5C60;  /* light muted — 4.50:1 on --bg-active #d4d4d8 (worst light) */
  --color-gray-600: #565453;  /* R-B=3 — transition zone cool→warm */
  --color-gray-700: #342E29;  /* R-B=11 — --color-border */
  --color-gray-800: #24201C;  /* R-B=8 — --color-surface */
  --color-gray-900: #171413;  /* R-B=4 — --color-bg */
  --color-gray-925: #100F0D;  /* R-B=3 — --color-inset */
  --color-gray-950: #090707;  /* R-B=2 — --color-overlay base */

  /* ===================
   * DESIGN TOKENS (24 Total)
   * =================== */

  /* Surfaces — warm charcoal (R-B=2-9). See the derivation block above.
     The bg→surface step is deliberately LARGER than the old default's (23→36 in
     luminance terms, against 38→46): that separation is most of what reads as
     "slick" in Dark (Warm), and it is the reason a widget card now sits off the
     page instead of merging with it. */
  --color-bg: #171413;
  --color-surface: #24201C;
  --color-surface-hover: #2B2522;
  --color-inset: #100F0D;
  --color-overlay: #090707;

  /* Text Hierarchy (Rule 4: Cool Tint B-R=1-4) */
  --color-heading: #F5F5F7;
  --color-body: #EDEDEF;
  --color-secondary: #A8A8AC;
  --color-muted: #838386;
  --color-placeholder: #7A7A7D;
  --color-disabled-text: #6B6968;

  /* Interactive */
  --color-brand: #FF7331;
  --color-brand-hover: #FF8855;
  --color-brand-active: #E5672C;
  --color-on-brand: #1A0A00;
  --color-link: #FF8C55;
  --color-link-hover: #FFA377;
  --color-focus-ring: #F5F5F7;

  /* Semantic */
  --color-error: #FF6B6B;
  --color-success: #44BF6E;
  --color-warning: #F5A623;

  /* Structural */
  --color-border: #342E29;
  --color-disabled-bg: #231F1D;
  --color-selection: #603722;

  /* ===================
   * BACKWARD COMPATIBILITY
   * =================== */

  /* Background */
  --bg-primary: var(--color-bg);
  --bg-secondary: var(--color-surface);
  --bg-tertiary: var(--color-surface);
  --bg-card: var(--color-surface);
  --bg-hover: var(--color-surface-hover);
  --bg-active: var(--color-surface-hover);
  --bg-elevated: var(--color-surface-hover);
  --bg-input: var(--color-inset);
  --bg-panel: var(--color-bg);

  /* Text */
  --text-primary: var(--color-body);
  --text-secondary: var(--color-secondary);
  /* STEP 11(c): was var(--color-muted) #838386, which fails AA on three of the four dark surfaces
   * (4.13 / 3.72 / 3.37 : 1 on --color-bg / --color-surface / --color-surface-hover). The palette
   * primitive --color-muted is UNCHANGED — it is exposed to Tailwind as `color-muted` and has
   * consumers outside this theme; only the semantic role moves. */
  --text-muted: var(--color-gray-450);

  /* Borders */
  --border-subtle: var(--color-border);
  --border-medium: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);
  --border-focus: var(--color-focus-ring);

  /* Accent (mapped to brand orange spec) */
  --accent-primary-rgb: 255, 115, 49;
  --accent-primary-hover-rgb: 255, 136, 85;
  --accent-primary-active-rgb: 229, 103, 44;
  --accent-success-rgb: 68, 191, 110;
  --accent-warning-rgb: 245, 166, 35;
  --accent-danger-rgb: 255, 107, 107;

  --accent-primary: var(--color-brand);
  --accent-primary-hover: var(--color-brand-hover);
  --accent-primary-active: var(--color-brand-active);
  --accent-success: var(--color-success);
  --accent-warning: var(--color-warning);
  --accent-danger: var(--color-error);
  --accent-ai: #a855f7;
  --accent-ai-rgb: 168, 85, 247;
  --accent-primary-subtle: rgba(var(--accent-primary-rgb), 0.1);
  --accent-primary-muted: rgba(var(--accent-primary-rgb), 0.6);

  /* Semantic text colors for positive/negative values */
  --text-positive: var(--accent-success);
  --text-negative: var(--accent-danger);

  /* Flat/unchanged indicator color */
  --neutral: var(--text-muted);

  /* New backward-compat tokens (9 new) */
  --bg-inset: var(--color-inset);
  --bg-disabled: var(--color-disabled-bg);
  --bg-overlay: var(--color-overlay);
  --text-heading: var(--color-heading);
  --text-placeholder: var(--color-placeholder);
  --text-link: var(--color-link);
  --text-link-hover: var(--color-link-hover);
  --text-disabled: var(--color-disabled-text);
  --focus-ring: var(--color-focus-ring);
  --selection-bg: var(--color-selection);

  /* Sidebar glass tint (defaults — overridden by [data-palette="warm"]).
     This is `--color-inset` expressed as rgba because the rails need the alpha for
     `backdrop-filter` to have anything to composite over; it tracked the old inset
     (29,26,25) and now tracks the new one. Kept in sync BY HAND — a `color-mix` or
     relative-colour form would resolve at use site and is not worth the indirection
     here, but if `--color-inset` moves again, this moves with it. */
  --sidebar-bg-collapsed: rgba(16, 15, 13, 0.85);
  --sidebar-bg-expanded: rgba(16, 15, 13, 0.85);

  /* Chart & UI Helper Tokens */
  --button-text-on-accent: var(--color-on-brand);
  --series-1: var(--color-brand);
  --grid-line: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);

  --font-size-xs: 11;

  /* ===================
   * Z-INDEX SCALE
   * Global: 0-150 (shell, widgets, modals, fullscreen)
   *   Headers/nav: 40-50, Modals: 100, Fullscreen: 150
   * Orion v3: 0-60 (scoped to .orion-v3 stacking context)
   *   NOTE: Radix portals render at <body>, bypassing .orion-v3 scope.
   *   Orion modals (z:60) may be eclipsed by global toasts (z:90).
   *   Mitigation: Radix uses built-in z-index management.
   * Analysis pane: 5-10 (scoped to analysis container)
   *
   * FOCUS RING: white (--border-focus → --color-focus-ring #F5F5F7) + 2px offset.
   * Offset ensures ring sits on background, not on element surface.
   * Visible even on orange buttons because ring-on-dark-bg ≈ 15:1 contrast.
   * =================== */
  --z-base: 0;
  /* The dashboard grid wrapper's own stacking context. Added 2026-08-10 (Step 11a): the sole
   * consumer, `widget-system/layout/grid-layout.tsx`, had been carrying a guessed literal
   * `var(--z-widget-grid, 1)` against a token that was defined nowhere in the repo — so the
   * guess was the only value doing any work. Defined here rather than in `apps/web` because
   * this block is the single authority for the z-scale; a second scale elsewhere is how the
   * two stop agreeing. Value 1 == the literal it replaces, so this is behaviour-preserving. */
  --z-widget-grid: 1;
  --z-widget-content: 1;
  --z-widget-header: 10;
  --z-sticky: 40;
  --z-dropdown: 50;
  --z-popover: 60;
  --z-tooltip: 70;
  --z-sidebar: 80;
  --z-toast: 90;
  --z-modal: 100;
  --z-fullscreen: 150;

  /* ===================
   * SHADOWS
   * =================== */
  --shadow-sm: 0 1px 2px 0 rgb(0 0 0 / 0.05);
  --shadow-card: 0 1px 3px 0 rgb(0 0 0 / 0.1), 0 1px 2px -1px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.1);
  --shadow-dropdown: 0 4px 6px -1px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.3), 0 2px 4px -2px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.3);
  --shadow-modal: 0 25px 50px -12px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.5);

  /* ===================
   * SPACING (for compact mode)
   * =================== */
  --spacing-unit: 1;
  --space-1: calc(4px * var(--spacing-unit));
  --space-2: calc(8px * var(--spacing-unit));
  --space-3: calc(12px * var(--spacing-unit));
  --space-4: calc(16px * var(--spacing-unit));
  --space-5: calc(20px * var(--spacing-unit));
  --space-6: calc(24px * var(--spacing-unit));
  --space-8: calc(32px * var(--spacing-unit));
  --space-10: calc(40px * var(--spacing-unit));
  --space-12: calc(48px * var(--spacing-unit));

  /* ===================
   * TYPOGRAPHY
   * =================== */
  --font-size-base: 16px;
  --font-sans: 'Roboto Flex', system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
  --font-mono: 'Roboto Mono', ui-monospace, 'Cascadia Code', monospace;

  /* Roboto Flex axis defaults (dark mode base) */
  --rf-wght: 400;
  --rf-wdth: 100;
  /* Compensate for dark-mode halation. Retuned with the surface family (`F-PALETTE-01`,
     2026-08-11): halation scales with the ink/ground gap, and this ground moved from
     #262322 to #171413 — a third of the way to Dark (Warm), which carries -40. So this
     moves the same third: -25 → -34. Leaving it at -25 would have let text bloom on a
     ground the value was never measured against. */
  --rf-grad: -34;
  --rf-ytlc: 510;   /* +2% x-height for screen legibility */
  --font-weight-normal: 400;
  --font-weight-medium: 500;
  --font-weight-semibold: 600;
  --font-weight-bold: 700;

  /* ===================
   * COMPONENT TOKENS
   * =================== */
  --button-bg: var(--accent-primary);
  --button-bg-hover: var(--accent-primary-hover);
  --button-bg-active: var(--accent-primary-active);
  --button-text: var(--button-text-on-accent);
  --button-secondary-bg: var(--bg-card);
  --button-secondary-border: var(--border-subtle);
  --button-secondary-hover: var(--bg-hover);
  --button-ghost-bg: transparent;
  --button-ghost-text: var(--text-secondary);
  --button-ghost-hover: var(--bg-hover);
  --button-danger-bg: var(--accent-danger);
  --button-danger-hover: rgb(220, 38, 38);

  --input-bg: var(--bg-input);
  --input-border: var(--border-medium);
  --input-focus: var(--border-focus);
  --input-text: var(--text-primary);
  --input-placeholder: var(--text-placeholder);

  /* ===================
   * LAYOUT TOKENS
   * =================== */
  --sidebar-collapsed: 48px;
  --sidebar-expanded-left: clamp(148px, 9vw, 172px);
  --sidebar-expanded-right: 216px;
  --sidebar-expanded: var(--sidebar-expanded-left);
  --sidebar-left-width: var(--sidebar-collapsed);
  --sidebar-transition: 200ms;
  --topbar-height: 0px;
  --bottombar-height: 64px;
  --statsbar-height: 24px;
  --bottombar-expanded-max: 50vh;
  --contextbar-height-compact: 40px;
  --contextbar-height-full: 56px;

  /* ===================
   * RADII
   * =================== */
  --radius-sm: 4px;
  --radius-md: 6px;
  --radius-lg: 8px;
  --radius-xl: 12px;
  --radius-full: 9999px;

  /* ===================
   * TRANSITIONS
   * =================== */
  --transition-fast: 150ms;
  --transition-normal: 200ms;
  --transition-slow: 300ms;
  --transition-ease: cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1);
  --transition-ease-out: cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
  --transition-spring: cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1);

  /* Easing tokens */
  --ease-morph: cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);
  --ease-enter: cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
  --ease-exit: cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.75, 0.4);
  --ease-standard: cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1);
  --ease-hover: cubic-bezier(0.25, 0, 0.5, 1);

  /* Panel background (between canvas and card) — alias to bg-primary */
  --bg-panel: var(--color-bg);

  /* Alpha-based border tokens (for CSS on dark backgrounds) */
  --border-alpha-faint: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.04);
  --border-alpha-subtle: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
  --border-alpha-medium: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
  --border-alpha-strong: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12);

  /* Scrollbar tokens */
  --scrollbar-width: 4px;
  --scrollbar-thumb: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
  --scrollbar-thumb-hover: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15);
  --scrollbar-track: transparent;

  /* Button text on accent backgrounds — WCAG AA compliant */
  --button-text-on-accent: #1A0A00;
}

/* ===================
 * LIGHT THEME
 * =================== */
.theme-light,
[data-theme="light"] {
  /* Light mode: no halation compensation */
  --rf-grad: 0;

  --bg-primary: #ffffff;
  --bg-secondary: var(--color-gray-100);
  --bg-card: #ffffff;
  --bg-hover: var(--color-gray-100);
  --bg-active: var(--color-gray-200);
  --bg-input: #ffffff;
  /* STEP 11(c): the light theme did not override --bg-elevated, so it INHERITED the dark
   * #353230 — a dark block in a light UI, carrying light-theme dark text at 1.91:1. It is used
   * at 9 sites inside widget-system, so it is inside this fold's surface. Raised to match
   * --bg-card, which is what "elevated" means in a light palette.
   * ⚠ --bg-tertiary, --bg-inset and --bg-overlay have the SAME gap and are deliberately NOT
   * fixed here: 0 of them are used in widget-system, and --bg-tertiary alone has ~304 consumers
   * across other programmes' pages. Routed in STEP11C-ROUTED-FINDINGS.md §(2). */
  --bg-elevated: #ffffff;

  --text-primary: var(--color-gray-950);
  --text-secondary: var(--color-gray-600);
  /* STEP 11(c): was var(--color-gray-400) #A8A8AC — 2.37 : 1 on white, 2.03 on --bg-secondary and
   * 1.60 on --bg-active. The light theme is live (theme-provider.tsx:43 and :112 follow the OS
   * colour scheme), so those values shipped to every light-mode user. gray-400 itself is unchanged. */
  --text-muted: var(--color-gray-550);

  --border-subtle: var(--color-gray-200);
  --border-medium: var(--color-gray-300);

  --shadow-dropdown: 0 4px 6px -1px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.1), 0 2px 4px -2px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.1);
  --shadow-modal: 0 25px 50px -12px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.25);

  --bg-panel: #f0f0f0;
  --border-alpha-faint: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.04);
  --border-alpha-subtle: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.06);
  --border-alpha-medium: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
  --border-alpha-strong: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);
  --scrollbar-thumb: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15);
  --scrollbar-thumb-hover: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25);

  /* Focus ring: dark on light bg for visibility */
  --color-focus-ring: #242323;

  /* Chart engine tokens — readable on white backgrounds */
  --up: #1a8a3e;
  --down: #c93c3c;
  --data-up: #1a8a3e;
  --data-down: #c93c3c;
  --data-up-bg: rgba(26, 138, 62, 0.1);
  --data-down-bg: rgba(201, 60, 60, 0.1);
  --series-1: #d97706;
  --series-2: #1d4ed8;
  --series-3: #15803d;
  --series-4: #b91c1c;
  --series-5: #7e22ce;
  --series-6: #c2410c;
  --series-7: #0e7490;
  --series-8: #4d7c0f;
  --grid-line: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.08);
}

/* ===================
 * ACCENT COLOR VARIANTS
 * =================== */
[data-accent="blue"] {
  --accent-primary-rgb: 59, 130, 246;
  --accent-primary-hover-rgb: 37, 99, 235;
  --accent-primary-active-rgb: 29, 78, 216;
  --color-brand: #3b82f6;
  --color-brand-hover: #2563eb;
  --color-brand-active: #1d4ed8;
  --color-on-brand: #FFFFFF;
  /* Button bg overrides: -600 base (5.19:1 AA w/ white), -500 hover (lighter feedback) */
  --button-bg: #2563EB;
  --button-bg-hover: #3b82f6;
  --button-bg-active: #1d4ed8;
}

[data-accent="green"] {
  --accent-primary-rgb: 34, 197, 94;
  --accent-primary-hover-rgb: 22, 163, 74;
  --accent-primary-active-rgb: 21, 128, 61;
  --color-brand: #22c55e;
  --color-brand-hover: #16a34a;
  --color-brand-active: #15803d;
  --color-on-brand: #052E16;
}

[data-accent="purple"] {
  --accent-primary-rgb: 168, 85, 247;
  --accent-primary-hover-rgb: 147, 51, 234;
  --accent-primary-active-rgb: 126, 34, 206;
  --color-brand: #a855f7;
  --color-brand-hover: #9333ea;
  --color-brand-active: #7e22ce;
  --color-on-brand: #FFFFFF;
  /* Button bg overrides: -600 base (5.37:1 AA w/ white), -500 hover (lighter feedback) */
  --button-bg: #9333EA;
